# File: tests/features/model-hub.feature
# Generated from: specs/5-replace-model-with-an-oh-my-pi-style-model-hub/requirements.md
Feature: oh-my-pi-style model hub for /model

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Hub lists Claude and logged-in providers, then dimmed ones
    Given stored logins for OpenCode Go and Codex, and xAI not logged in
    When the user runs "/model"
    Then the hub shows "All models", Claude, OpenCode Go and Codex with counts, then a dimmed xAI entry

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Rows and the detail line show capabilities
    Given the hub is open on OpenCode Go
    When a row is highlighted
    Then the row shows id, current mark, context, price and speed, and the detail line shows name, context, max out, price, reasoning and vision

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Search ranks matches across providers
    Given the hub is open
    When the user types "kimi"
    Then matching models are listed by match quality then recent use, and entries without matches are dimmed and cannot be chosen

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Selecting a model switches it and keeps the conversation
    Given a conversation on a Claude model
    When the user selects "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" and later "opus"
    Then each pick runs Claude Code's own /model switch for that id

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A provider without credentials hands off to login
    Given the dimmed xAI entry
    When the user presses Enter and then "Log in to xAI"
    Then the pane shows xAI has no credentials with its catalog preview, the login flow runs, and the hub reopens on xAI

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Arguments switch directly, first open refreshes, and Esc clears then closes
    Given "/model opus"
    When the command runs, and later the hub opens a provider and Esc is pressed twice with a search typed
    Then the switch runs without the hub, the provider refreshes once, the first Esc clears the search and the second closes the hub

  @SCN007
  Scenario: A smaller context window compacts before switching
    Given a transcript larger than a routed model's context window
    When the user selects that model
    Then its row showed a context-too-large mark, the session compacts, and then the model switches

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Settings rows follow the catalog
    Given discovered routed models and a settings file with the user's own rows
    When the catalog refreshes
    Then modelPicker.options keeps the user's rows and adds one provider-labeled row per enabled routed model
